From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:41:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [gbinder] Don't record offsets of NULL buffer objects.

libhwbinder writes a buffer object with a NULL address into the parcel
data but leaves it out of the object offsets (Parcel::writeObject), so
the binder driver never translates it and the parent's pointer stays
NULL. An empty hidl_vec or a NULL hidl_string therefore reaches a HIDL
service as a NULL pointer.

libgbinder recorded every buffer object. The driver then pointed the
empty buffer into the target's transaction buffer, and the service saw
a non-NULL pointer of length 0. Trustonic's Gatekeeper HAL
(gatekeeper.trustonic.so) accepts a first enrolment only when the
current password and handle are NULL, so every enroll() from libgbinder
with empty vectors failed with ERROR_INVALID (-1), while the same call
from Android's gatekeeperd succeeded against the same HAL.

Skip the offset for a NULL buffer, as is already done for NULL binder
objects.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/gbinder_writer.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gbinder_writer.c b/src/gbinder_writer.c
index 6d59ffa..041754b 100644
--- a/src/gbinder_writer.c
+++ b/src/gbinder_writer.c
@@ -950,8 +950,19 @@ gbinder_writer_data_append_buffer_object(
     n = data->io->encode_buffer_object(buf->data + offset, ptr, size, parent);
     /* Fix the data size */
     g_byte_array_set_size(buf, offset + n);
-    /* Record the offset */
-    gbinder_writer_data_record_offset(data, offset);
+    /*
+     * Record the offset, but not for a NULL buffer. libhwbinder writes
+     * such an object into the data but leaves it out of the offsets
+     * (Parcel::writeObject), so the driver never translates it and the
+     * pointer in the parent (e.g. an empty hidl_vec) stays NULL on the
+     * receiving side. Recorded, the driver would point it at the target's
+     * buffer and the receiver would see a non-NULL pointer of length 0,
+     * which some HALs reject (Trustonic Gatekeeper's enroll() takes a
+     * first enrolment only when the current password is NULL).
+     */
+    if (ptr) {
+        gbinder_writer_data_record_offset(data, offset);
+    }
     /* The driver seems to require each buffer to be 8-byte aligned */
     data->buffers_size += G_ALIGN8(size);
     return index;
-- 
